			Therefore, DbContext should be Scoped.
			
  
What is asp.net core ?
	ASP.NET Core is a cross-platform framework from Microsoft used to build web applications, Web APIs, and backend services.
	It is fast, lightweight, and supports features like Dependency Injection, Middleware, Routing, and Authentication.
	For example, we can use ASP.NET Core to build a Web API for an Angular application.


.net framework vs .net :
  .NET Framework is the older Microsoft platform, mainly used for Windows applications and older ASP.NET applications.
  .NET is the newer, cross-platform platform that runs on Windows, Linux, and macOS.
  .NET is faster, more modern, and supports technologies like ASP.NET Core, Web API, and modern cloud applications.
  So, .NET Framework = older and mainly Windows, .NET = modern and cross-platform.


What is Kestrel :
  Kestrel is the default cross-platform web server used by ASP.NET Core applications. 
  It receives HTTP requests and sends responses back to the client.
  For example, when we run an ASP.NET Core Web API,
  Kestrel listens on a port like https://localhost:5001 and handles the requests.
  
  
